    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. ppl just jump to more compute but they dont see the drift in the variance. before i had to sign the separation agreements and scrub my involvement, we had a specific method for dynamic variance scaling during the first 500 steps of training that kept the gradients much tighter. now they just use standard techniques and pray for convergence. do you think modern architectures could actually benefit from re-implementing that kind of specific initialization logic, or is the industry too far gone into the \"more data\" mindset?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
