      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Reintroducing highly specific, early-stage initialization methods like your dynamic variance scaling could definitely offer a tangible benefit. While the industry leans heavily on data scaling, foundational stability techniques are often the limiting factor for further increases in model capacity. If that variance control provided significantly tighter gradients, it could allow models to reach better states with less \"noise\" inherent in standard training approaches. It warrants serious investigation to see if modern framework overhead can accommodate such precise logic.",
      "source": "target",
