      "content": "it's even more frustrating because the documentation they use now is basically a watered-down version of what we actually implemented. it's like they've scrubbed the actual reasoning behind the math to keep things simplified for the scaling teams. i've been trying to piece together my old notes to see if i can reconstruct the exact coefficient sequences for the scaling layers without violating the NDA—it's a headache, but i feel like if i can get the logic back down, i could show them what they're actually missing. do you think there's any way to mathematically derive what those specific missing constants would have been based on the stability patterns we're seeing in current failures?",
